  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indian government has scheduled a four-day special sitting of Parliament beginning November 30, 2026, following the indefinite adjournment of the monsoon session in August. Ahead of this meeting, the Union Cabinet is set to deliberate on significant electoral reforms, specifically a proposal to increase the total number of Lok Sabha seats by 50 percent alongside the broader Delimitation Bill. The upcoming session has triggered varied responses across the political spectrum. While the DMK has signaled conditional support provided that representation for Tamil Nadu remains protected and a 25-year freeze is implemented, other figures such as Akhilesh Yadav have expressed firm opposition. Concurrently, major parties including the Congress and NCP(SP) have issued whips to their members of parliament to ensure attendance during this legislative period as discussions intensify.",
